cross/xcode-build/ -- Apple toolchain resolution for the iOS cross-build.

This directory holds the small amount of shell glue needed for the
recursive XCONFIGURE=ios configure invocation to find Apple's clang,
the iOS SDK, and the right -arch / -isysroot / -mios-version-min flags
to pass for an iOS target.

It exists for the same reason cross/ndk-build/ exists for Android:
the outer ./configure --with-ios run is an ordinary host build that
does not produce iOS code; it re-invokes itself with XCONFIGURE=ios
to do the actual cross-compile.  The recursive invocation needs to be
told which compiler to use.  Rather than open-code that logic in
configure.ac, it is consolidated here so it can be tested
independently and so a curious reader has a single place to look.

Unlike the NDK port, iOS has nothing analogous to Android's ndk-build
Make-based build system, so this directory is intentionally tiny --
one sourceable shell helper.

Files:

  xcode-toolchain.sh
        Sourceable POSIX shell script.  When sourced (with $IOS_SDK
        and $IOS_ARCH optionally set, and $IOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
        required), exports CC, CXX, AR, RANLIB, CFLAGS, LDFLAGS,
        OBJCFLAGS for an iOS cross-compile.  Errors out if not on
        macOS or if xcrun cannot resolve the requested SDK.

Environment variables consumed:

  IOS_SDK          Either "iphoneos" (device, default) or
                   "iphonesimulator" (Simulator).
  IOS_ARCH         CPU arch.  Defaults to arm64 for both SDKs;
                   x86_64 is also valid for iphonesimulator on Intel
                   Macs.
  IOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
                   Minimum iOS version, e.g. 15.0.  Required.

Environment variables exported:

  CC, CXX, AR, RANLIB
                   Resolved via `xcrun --sdk $IOS_SDK -f ...'.
  CFLAGS, OBJCFLAGS, LDFLAGS
                   Augmented (not replaced) with -arch, -isysroot,
                   and the appropriate -m*-version-min flag.

This script is invoked by the recursive XCONFIGURE=ios configure path
in configure.ac.  It can also be sourced by hand for debugging:

  IOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=15.0 . cross/xcode-build/xcode-toolchain.sh
  $CC --version
